<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Clustering in practice</title>
<meta name="description" content="A visual introduction to clustering in unsupervised machine learning.">
<meta name="author" content="Nick White">
<link rel="canonical" href="https://nickwhite.cc/talks/clustering-in-practice/">
<meta property="og:type" content="article">
<meta property="og:title" content="Clustering in practice">
<meta property="og:description" content="A visual introduction to clustering in unsupervised machine learning.">
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/reveal.js@5.1.0/dist/reset.css" integrity="sha384-AJKv9Ui5SfA0VsFksFI9GuA1ztX9Ca3CLP6HGfX4YY/tYSVodC+PUszaQZFIlkuy" crossorigin="anonymous">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/reveal.js@5.1.0/dist/reveal.css" integrity="sha384-YgvgKeZJykuztG+iQPoZHNZENTFZvOcOJ/uRzmJTje6GHYN9zAw+y5rx/L8MQKA/" crossorigin="anonymous">
<style>
/* ---- deck theme ---- */
:root {
  --ink: #27272a;
  --ink-soft: #52525b;
  --accent: #2a78d6;
  --line: #e4e4e7;
  --grey-dot: #d4d4d8;
}
.reveal-viewport { background: #fafafa; }
.reveal { font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, "Apple Color Emoji", "Segoe UI Emoji", "Segoe UI Symbol", "Noto Color Emoji"; color: var(--ink); font-size: 40px; }
.reveal .slides section { text-align: left; }
.reveal h1, .reveal h2 { font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, "Apple Color Emoji", "Segoe UI Emoji", "Segoe UI Symbol", "Noto Color Emoji"; color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: none; }
.reveal .rule { height: 8px; width: 4.5em; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 4px; margin: 0.4em 0 0.7em; }
.reveal h1 { font-size: 2.1em; }
.reveal h2 { font-size: 1.25em; margin-bottom: 0.4em; }
.reveal .soft { color: var(--ink-soft); }
.reveal a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.12em; }
.reveal a:hover { text-decoration: none; }
.reveal .closing p { margin: 0 0 0.5em; }
.reveal .closing ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.3em; }
.reveal .closing li { margin-bottom: 0.3em; }
.reveal .cols { display: flex; gap: 0.8em; align-items: stretch; }

/* ---- journey dot field ---- */
.reveal .viz { position: relative; }
.reveal .gfield { position: relative; width: 980px; height: 560px; }
.reveal .vstep { position: absolute; width: 0; height: 0; }
.reveal .gdot {
  position: absolute; width: 16px; height: 16px; border-radius: 50%;
  box-sizing: border-box; background: var(--grey-dot);
  z-index: 2;
}
.reveal .gdot.sq { border-radius: 3.5px; }
.reveal .gdot.tri { border-radius: 0; width: 18px; height: 17px; clip-path: polygon(50% 4%, 100% 96%, 0% 96%); }
.reveal .gdot.dia { border-radius: 3.5px; transform: rotate(45deg); }
.reveal .legend { display: flex; gap: 1.1em; align-items: center; font-size: 0.5em; color: var(--ink-soft); font-weight: 500; margin-top: 0.45em; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.reveal .legend .gdot { position: static; display: inline-block; vertical-align: -2px; margin-right: 8px; background: #a1a1aa; }

/* ---- toy SVG machinery ---- */
.reveal .toysvg { display: block; margin: 0 auto; overflow: visible; }
.reveal .toysvg .tdot { fill: var(--grey-dot); transition: fill 0.6s, opacity 0.6s, stroke-width 0.45s; }
.reveal .toysvg text { font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, "Apple Color Emoji", "Segoe UI Emoji", "Segoe UI Symbol", "Noto Color Emoji"; }
.reveal .toysvg .tmark { transform: translate(var(--x0), var(--y0)); transition: transform 1.1s ease, opacity 0.5s; }
.reveal .toysvg .lset { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.7s; }
.reveal .toysvg .candg { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.6s; }

/* the running-total table */
.reveal .meter { position: absolute; right: 24px; top: 24px; width: 320px; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.5s; z-index: 8; }
.reveal .meter .mlabel { font-size: 0.42em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); text-align: right; border-bottom: 2.5px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 6px; }
.reveal .meter .mrow { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.45s; padding-top: 8px; }
.reveal .meter .mrow .mk { font-size: 0.42em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink-soft); }
.reveal .meter .mrow .mvv { font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, "Apple Color Emoji", "Segoe UI Emoji", "Segoe UI Symbol", "Noto Color Emoji"; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 700; }

/* ---- slide 2: example personas (static, no fragments) ---- */
.reveal .viz-recap .gfield .gdot { background: var(--k4); }

/* ---- slide 3: k means clustering ---- */
.reveal .pcard {
  background: #fff; border: 2.5px solid var(--pc); border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 0.4em 0.6em; margin-bottom: 0.55em; position: relative;
}
.reveal .pcard .pname { font-weight: 700; color: var(--pc-text, var(--pc)); font-size: 0.62em; }
.reveal .pcard .ptraits { font-size: 0.47em; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 2px; }
.reveal .pcard .pbar { height: 14px; border-radius: 7px; background: var(--pc); width: var(--bw); margin-top: 10px; }
.reveal .pcard .prate { position: absolute; right: 14px; bottom: 10px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--pc-text, var(--pc)); font-size: 0.55em; }

/* the meter occupies 344px on the right (320px + 24px inset); shifting the
   centred svg left by half of that centres it in the space the meter leaves */
.reveal .viz-lloyd .toysvg { transform: translateX(-172px); }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .toysvg .tmark { opacity: 0; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k1.visible ~ .toysvg .tmark { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k2.visible ~ .toysvg .candg { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k3.visible ~ .toysvg .candg { opacity: 0; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k3.visible ~ .toysvg .ls0 { opacity: 0.5; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k3.visible ~ .toysvg .tdot { fill: var(--c0); }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k3.visible ~ .meter { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k3.visible ~ .meter .mr1 { opacity: 1; }
/* k4: lines clear, centroids move to the mean of their current cluster — no re-measure yet */
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k4.visible ~ .toysvg .tmark { transform: translate(var(--x1), var(--y1)); }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k4.visible ~ .toysvg .ls0 { opacity: 0; }
/* k5: re-measure from the new positions — new lines, reassigned colours, meter falls */
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k5.visible ~ .toysvg .ls1 { opacity: 0.5; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k5.visible ~ .toysvg .tdot { fill: var(--c1); }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k5.visible ~ .meter .mr1 { opacity: 0.5; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k5.visible ~ .meter .mr2 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k6.visible ~ .toysvg .tmark { transform: translate(var(--x2), var(--y2)); }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k6.visible ~ .toysvg .ls1 { opacity: 0; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k6.visible ~ .toysvg .ls2 { opacity: 0.5; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k6.visible ~ .toysvg .tdot { fill: var(--c2); }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k6.visible ~ .meter .mr2 { opacity: 0.5; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k6.visible ~ .meter .mr3 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k7.visible ~ .toysvg .tmark { transform: translate(var(--xf), var(--yf)); }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k7.visible ~ .toysvg .ls2 { opacity: 0; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k7.visible ~ .toysvg .tdot { fill: var(--cf); }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k7.visible ~ .meter .mr3 { opacity: 0.5; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k7.visible ~ .meter .mr4 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .capstack { margin-top: 0.3em; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .capstack .cap { display: none; font-size: 0.62em; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .capstack .cap0 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k1.visible ~ .capstack .cap0 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k1.visible ~ .capstack .cap1 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k2.visible ~ .capstack .cap1 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k2.visible ~ .capstack .cap2 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k3.visible ~ .capstack .cap2 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k3.visible ~ .capstack .cap3 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k4.visible ~ .capstack .cap3 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k4.visible ~ .capstack .cap4 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k5.visible ~ .capstack .cap4 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k5.visible ~ .capstack .cap5 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k6.visible ~ .capstack .cap5 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k6.visible ~ .capstack .cap6 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k7.visible ~ .capstack .cap6 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-lloyd .k7.visible ~ .capstack .cap7 { display: block; }

/* ---- slide 5: extreme values ---- */
.reveal .primer-svg { display: block; margin: 0 auto; overflow: visible; }
.reveal .primer-svg text { font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, "Apple Color Emoji", "Segoe UI Emoji", "Segoe UI Symbol", "Noto Color Emoji"; }
.reveal .primer-svg .tdotp { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-40px); transition: opacity 0.45s, transform 0.6s cubic-bezier(.3,1.4,.5,1); }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p1.visible ~ .primer-svg .td1 { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p1.visible ~ .primer-svg .td2 { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
.reveal .primer-svg .mmean, .reveal .primer-svg .mmed { transition: transform 1.0s ease; }
.reveal .primer-svg .mmean { transform: translateX(var(--px0)); }
.reveal .primer-svg .mmed { transform: translateX(var(--qx0)); }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p1.visible ~ .primer-svg .mmean { transform: translateX(var(--px2)); }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p1.visible ~ .primer-svg .mmed { transform: translateX(var(--qx2)); }
.reveal .primer-svg .mval { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.4s; }
.reveal .primer-svg .mval.v0 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p1.visible ~ .primer-svg .mval.v0 { opacity: 0; }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p1.visible ~ .primer-svg .mval.v2 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .dragsvg .dmark { transform: translate(var(--x0), var(--y0)); transition: transform 1.1s ease, opacity 0.4s; }
.reveal .dragsvg .mring { transform: translate(var(--x0), var(--y0)); transition: transform 1.1s ease, opacity 0.4s; }
.reveal .dragsvg .odot { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-46px); transition: opacity 0.5s, transform 0.7s cubic-bezier(.3,1.3,.5,1); }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p3.visible ~ .dragwrap .dragsvg .odot { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p3.visible ~ .dragwrap .dragsvg .dmark { transform: translate(var(--x1), var(--y1)); }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p3.visible ~ .dragwrap .dragsvg .mring { transform: translate(var(--x1), var(--y1)); }
.reveal .draglegend { position: absolute; right: 24px; bottom: 10px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4em; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 0.5em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink-soft); z-index: 8; }
.reveal .draglegend svg { vertical-align: -5px; margin-right: 9px; }
.reveal .viz-extreme .capstack { margin-top: 0.4em; }
.reveal .viz-extreme .capstack .cap { display: none; font-size: 0.62em; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); }
.reveal .viz-extreme .capstack .cap0 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p1.visible ~ .capstack .cap0 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p1.visible ~ .capstack .cap1 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p3.visible ~ .capstack .cap1 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-extreme .p3.visible ~ .capstack .cap2 { display: block; }

/* ---- slide 6: sensitivity, two strips ---- */
.reveal .sens-svg { display: block; margin: 0 auto; overflow: visible; }
.reveal .sens-svg text { font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, "Apple Color Emoji", "Segoe UI Emoji", "Segoe UI Symbol", "Noto Color Emoji"; }
.reveal .viz-sens .cap { font-size: 0.62em; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 0.4em; }

/* ---- slide 7: it never says no ---- */
.reveal .stack { position: relative; width: 980px; height: 560px; margin: 0 auto; transform: scale(0.92); transform-origin: top left; }
.reveal .stack .toysvg { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; }
.reveal .viz-never .svgA .tdot { fill: var(--s0); }
.reveal .viz-never .svgA .mgrp { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.5s; }
.reveal .viz-never .svgA .mg0 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-never .n1.visible ~ .stack .svgA .tdot { fill: var(--s1); }
.reveal .viz-never .n1.visible ~ .stack .svgA .mg0 { opacity: 0; }
.reveal .viz-never .n1.visible ~ .stack .svgA .mg1 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-never .n2.visible ~ .stack .svgA .tdot { fill: var(--s2); }
.reveal .viz-never .n2.visible ~ .stack .svgA .mg1 { opacity: 0; }
.reveal .viz-never .n2.visible ~ .stack .svgA .mg2 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-never .n3.visible ~ .stack .svgA .tdot { fill: var(--s3); }
.reveal .viz-never .n3.visible ~ .stack .svgA .mg2 { opacity: 0; }
.reveal .viz-never .n3.visible ~ .stack .svgA .mg3 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-never .n4.visible ~ .stack .svgA .tdot { fill: var(--s4); }
.reveal .viz-never .n4.visible ~ .stack .svgA .mg3 { opacity: 0; }
.reveal .viz-never .n4.visible ~ .stack .svgA .mg4 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .kchart { position: absolute; right: -10px; top: 10px; width: 380px; z-index: 8; }
.reveal .kchart .cp, .reveal .kchart .cs { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.45s; }
.reveal .kchart .cp0 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-never .n1.visible ~ .kchart .cp1, .reveal .viz-never .n1.visible ~ .kchart .cs1 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-never .n2.visible ~ .kchart .cp2, .reveal .viz-never .n2.visible ~ .kchart .cs2 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-never .n3.visible ~ .kchart .cp3, .reveal .viz-never .n3.visible ~ .kchart .cs3 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-never .n4.visible ~ .kchart .cp4, .reveal .viz-never .n4.visible ~ .kchart .cs4 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-never .cap { font-size: 0.62em; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 0.3em; }
.reveal .viz-never .cap p { margin: 0 0 0.6em; }
/* ---- slide 7: how do we fix that ---- */
.reveal .curvelabel { font-size: 0.5em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0.2em 0 0.1em 0.3em; }
.reveal .viz-fix .fixwrap { transform: scale(0.84); transform-origin: top center; margin-bottom: -86px; }
.reveal .viz-fix .cap { font-size: 0.62em; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 0.5em; }
.reveal .viz-fix .cap p { margin: 0 0 0.6em; }
.reveal .minifield .curvelabel { text-align: center; margin: 0; }

/* ---- slide 8: any clusters at all ---- */
.reveal .viz-noisefit .nfmarks { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.5s; }
.reveal .viz-noisefit .a1.visible ~ .nfsvg .tdot { fill: var(--nf); }
.reveal .viz-noisefit .a1.visible ~ .nfsvg .nfmarks { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-noisefit .a1.visible ~ .meter { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-noisefit .a1.visible ~ .meter .mr1 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-noisefit .capstack { margin-top: 0.4em; }
.reveal .viz-noisefit .capstack .cap { display: none; font-size: 0.62em; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); }
.reveal .viz-noisefit .capstack .cap0 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-noisefit .a1.visible ~ .capstack .cap0 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-noisefit .a1.visible ~ .capstack .cap1 { display: block; }

/* ---- slide 9: resample, refit ---- */
.reveal .shakebox { position: relative; }
.reveal .viz-shake .shakesvg .tdot { fill: var(--b0); }
.reveal .jtab { margin: 0.3em 0.3em 0; font-size: 0.42em; font-weight: 700; }
.reveal .jtab .jline { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.9em; margin-top: 7px; }
.reveal .jtab .jbar { flex: 1; display: flex; height: 24px; border-radius: 6px; overflow: hidden; }
.reveal .jtab .jbar span { height: 100%; }
.reveal .jtab .jsc { width: 4.6em; text-align: right; font-size: 1.15em; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.reveal .jtab .jv { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.5s; }
.reveal .viz-shake .r1.visible ~ .cols .jv1 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-shake .r2.visible ~ .cols .jv2 { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-shake .r3.visible ~ .cols .jv3 { opacity: 1; }
/* the scores arrive together on the final click, after all three bars */
.reveal .jtab .jnum { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.5s; }
.reveal .viz-shake .r4.visible ~ .cols .jnum { opacity: 1; }
.reveal .viz-shake .r1.visible ~ .cols .shakesvg .tdot { fill: var(--b1); opacity: var(--o1); stroke: rgba(39,39,42,0.55); stroke-width: var(--w1); }
.reveal .viz-shake .r2.visible ~ .cols .shakesvg .tdot { fill: var(--b2); opacity: var(--o2); stroke: rgba(39,39,42,0.55); stroke-width: var(--w2); }
.reveal .viz-shake .r3.visible ~ .cols .shakesvg .tdot { fill: var(--b3); opacity: var(--o3); stroke: rgba(39,39,42,0.55); stroke-width: var(--w3); }
.reveal .viz-shake .capstack { margin-top: 0.4em; }
.reveal .viz-shake .capstack .cap { display: none; font-size: 0.62em; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); }
.reveal .viz-shake .capstack .cap0 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-shake .r1.visible ~ .capstack .cap0 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-shake .r1.visible ~ .capstack .cap1 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-shake .r2.visible ~ .capstack .cap1 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-shake .r2.visible ~ .capstack .cap2 { display: block; }
.reveal .viz-shake .r4.visible ~ .capstack .cap2 { display: none; }
.reveal .viz-shake .r4.visible ~ .capstack .cap3 { display: block; }
</style>

<style>
/* notes written onto the slides */
.reveal .prose { font-size: 0.55em; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); }
.reveal .prose p { margin: 0 0 0.75em; }
.reveal .subtitle { font-size: 0.75em; max-width: 36em; line-height: 1.4; margin: 0 0 0.6em; }
.reveal .prose-title { max-width: 36em; margin-top: 0; }
.reveal .prose-below { max-width: 1500px; margin-top: 1.1em; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="reveal">
<div class="slides">
<section>
  <h1>Who is searching on my hotel?</h1>
  <div class="rule"></div>
  <p class="soft subtitle">A visual introduction to unsupervised machine learning.</p>
  <div class="prose prose-title"><p>Premise, structure, and all words by Nick White. Animations by Claude.</p></div>
</section>

<section>
    <div class="viz viz-recap">
    <div class="cols" style="transform: scale(0.82); transform-origin: top left; margin-bottom: -104px">
      <div style="flex: 0 0 62%">
        <div class="gfield" style="transform: scale(0.92); transform-origin: top left">{{ field_recap }}</div>
        <div class="legend">
          <span><span class="gdot"></span>solo</span>
          <span><span class="gdot sq"></span>couple</span>
          <span><span class="gdot tri"></span>family</span>
          <span><span class="gdot dia"></span>group</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="flex: 1">
{{ cards }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="prose prose-below">
      <p>Here's a simplified version of a system my team built recently. The company runs scripts on hotel websites and wanted to analyse the resulting data about (anonymised) website users, such as their rough location, room search history on the website, and what interest-specific pages they might have browsed. We wanted to use this to help our customers, who are mostly non-technical, get a broader idea of what kinds of people were searching and booking.</p>
      <p>To achieve this, we need to look for groups and similarities in the data. One way of achieving this is using a technique called clustering.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="viz viz-lloyd">
    <span class="fragment vstep k1"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep k2"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep k3"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep k4"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep k5"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep k6"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep k7"></span>
    <svg class="toysvg" width="980" height="560" viewBox="0 0 980 560">
{{ toy_lloyd }}
    </svg>
    <div class="meter"><div class="mlabel">total distance</div>{{ meter_lloyd }}</div>
    <div class="capstack">
<p class="cap cap0">Let's start with an example of some data points. To a human, it pretty obviously contains three main clusters. How do we get a machine to see them too?</p>
<p class="cap cap1">We start by dropping three crosses (called centroids) completely at random.</p>
<p class="cap cap2">For each point, we measure its distance to every centroid, and keep the nearest.</p>
<p class="cap cap3">We then sum all points' distances to their nearest centroid. The goal of clustering is to minimise that total distance number.</p>
<p class="cap cap4">We then move each cross to the average position (i.e. the centre) of the points it just claimed.</p>
<p class="cap cap5">Then we repeat the measurement. We can see the distance has gone down a bit.</p>
<p class="cap cap6">And now it's gone down a bit more.</p>
<p class="cap cap7">We're done when the distance stops falling when we update the centroids.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="viz viz-extreme">
    <span class="fragment vstep p1"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep p3"></span>
    <svg class="primer-svg" width="1350" height="264" viewBox="0 0 1480 290">
{{ primer }}
    </svg>
    <div class="dragwrap" style="position: relative; margin-top: -0.1em">
      <svg class="toysvg dragsvg" width="666" height="380" viewBox="0 0 980 560" style="display:block;margin:0 auto">
{{ drag }}
      </svg>
      <div class="draglegend" aria-label="centre statistic legend">
        <span><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="-14 -14 28 28"><path d="M-9,-9 L9,9 M-9,9 L9,-9" stroke="#27272a" stroke-width="5.5" stroke-linecap="round" fill="none"/></svg>mean (sensitive measure)</span>
        <span><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="-14 -14 28 28"><circle r="9.5" fill="none" stroke="#27272a" stroke-width="4.5"/></svg>medoid (resistant measure)</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="capstack">
<p class="cap cap0">Clustering is a powerful technique, but it has a few gotchas we must be aware of. One such is the definition of 'average' in the sentence 'we move each cross to the average of its points'.</p><p class="cap cap0">Two common definitions, seen here, are mean and medoid.</p>
<p class="cap cap1">When we introduce a few large values to the dataset, the mean shifts but the medoid doesn't. Because of this behaviour, we call the mean a 'sensitive' measure and the medoid a 'resistant' one.</p>
<p class="cap cap2">Adding a few outliers to the blue cluster produces the same behaviour: the sensitive mean (X) shifts more than the medoid (O).</p><p class="cap cap2">A memory aid I use for this is: "Mean people are actually really sensitive."</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="viz viz-sens">
    <svg class="sens-svg sens-top" width="1350" height="366" viewBox="0 0 1480 400">
{{ value_strip }}
    </svg>
    <p class="cap">Often, knowing which average to use comes down to the context of the problem. In this case, with booking value data, many guests didn't book (so their booking value is $0) but a handful did. We definitely want the sensitive measure, as we want the difference that those bookers make to the hotelier's bottom line to be reflected in the clusters.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="viz viz-never">
    <span class="fragment vstep n1"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep n2"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep n3"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep n4"></span>
    <div class="stack">
      <svg class="toysvg svgA" width="980" height="560" viewBox="0 0 980 560">
{{ never }}
      </svg>
    </div>
    <div class="kchart">
      <div class="mlabel" style="font-size: 0.42em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft)">total distance per k</div>
      <svg class="toysvg" width="380" height="270" viewBox="0 0 380 270">{{ kchart }}</svg>
    </div>
  <div class="cap"><p>Another thing I glossed over earlier was how we picked the number of clusters we want (which we call "k"). In that example we chose k=3, and there happened to be 3 clear clusters. How do you know the right number to choose when you can't eyeball the data?</p><p>This example illustrates how higher k always produces lower distance numbers, making higher k look naively like a "better" fit even when they are clearly not.</p></div></div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="viz viz-fix">
    <div class="fixwrap">
    <svg class="toysvg fixcurve" width="980" height="300" viewBox="0 0 980 300">
{{ curve }}
    </svg>
    <div class="cols" style="width: 1240px; margin: 0.25em auto 0; gap: 2.2em">
      <div class="minifield mf3" style="flex: 1">
        <div class="curvelabel">{{ label_k3 }}</div>
        <svg class="toysvg" width="480" height="274" viewBox="0 0 980 560">{{ mini_k3 }}</svg>
      </div>
      <div class="minifield mf7" style="flex: 1">
        <div class="curvelabel">{{ label_k7 }}</div>
    </div>
        <svg class="toysvg" width="480" height="274" viewBox="0 0 980 560">{{ mini_k7 }}</svg>
      </div>
    </div>
  <div class="cap"><p>When we don't know how to choose k, one option is to do what's called a k-sweep. The optimum k will often be where the decrease in distance in between each increment stops decreasing quite as much. This is known as the knee and it's much easier to visualise than explain in words.</p><p>Going way past the knee means overfitting, which is a technical term for "not seeing the wood for the trees."</p></div></div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="viz viz-noisefit">
    <span class="fragment vstep a1"></span>
    <svg class="toysvg nfsvg" width="924" height="528" viewBox="0 0 980 560" style="display:block;margin:0 auto">
{{ noisefit }}
    </svg>
    <div class="meter"><div class="mlabel">total distance</div>{{ meter_noise }}</div>
  <div class="capstack">
<p class="cap cap0">There are several other variants of the clustering-will-always-give-you-an-answer trap. Here are some points that I generated purely randomly. We can see intuitively that there are no meaningful clusters in this data.</p>
<p class="cap cap1">But if you run with it anyway... you will still get clusters, just meaningless ones!</p>
    </div></div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="viz viz-shake">
    <span class="fragment vstep r1"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep r2"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep r3"></span>
    <span class="fragment vstep r4"></span>
    <div class="cols" style="margin-top: 0.2em">
      <div class="shakebox" style="flex: 1">
        <svg class="toysvg shakesvg" width="560" height="320" viewBox="0 0 980 560">{{ shake_toy }}</svg>
        <div class="jtab">{{ jtab_toy }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="shakebox" style="flex: 1">
        <svg class="toysvg shakesvg" width="560" height="320" viewBox="0 0 980 560">{{ shake_noise }}</svg>
        <div class="jtab">{{ jtab_noise }}</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  <div class="capstack">
<p class="cap cap0">Fortunately, there are some standard checks for this. One such check is: what happens if you take a random sample of the points and rerun clustering on it? Do you have roughly the same groups or are the groups completely different?</p>
<p class="cap cap1">Here's an example: we've refit clusters on not every single point but only a subset of them.</p>
<p class="cap cap2">When we do this a few times, we can see on the left that the clusters roughly stayed in the same groups for the different subsamples, but on the right, the groups were shifting around a lot. This is known as cluster stability.</p>
<p class="cap cap3">There's a numeric measure of this as well as a visual one, called the Jaccard index. (1 is perfectly stable and 0 is entirely unstable.) <br/> This family of checks, where we re-run the algorithm with slight tweaks and see how much the result changes, is called bootstrapping.</p>
    </div></div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Thanks for reading</h2>
  <div class="rule"></div>
  <div class="soft closing" style="max-width: 36em; margin-bottom: 0.5em; font-size: 0.62em">
  <p>This was an introduction to clustering. The main things to remember are:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Clustering is a powerful way to spot groups or commonalities in large amounts of data.</li>
    <li>However, clustering always gives you an answer. It's on you to check the answer is meaningful, stable, and valuable in context.</li>
  </ul>
  </div>
  <p class="soft" style="font-size: 0.7em"><a href="/blog/">Back to the blog</a></p>

</section>

